## Common Pitfalls to Avoid

❌ **DON'T:**
```javascript
// Storing secrets in code
const JWT_SECRET = 'my-secret-key';

// Exposing stack traces
app.use((err, req, res) => {
  res.json({ error: err.stack });
});

// Trusting client input
app.post('/users', (req, res) => {
  db.insert(req.body); // Dangerous!
});

// Allowing all origins
app.use(cors()); // No options = allows ALL

// Logging sensitive data
console.log(req.body); // May contain passwords!

// Using synchronous operations
const data = fs.readFileSync(file);
```

✅ **DO:**
```javascript
// Use environment variables
const JWT_SECRET = process.env.JWT_SECRET;

// Hide stack traces in production
const message = NODE_ENV === 'production' 
  ? 'Internal Server Error' 
  : err.stack;

// Validate and sanitize
const validated = validator.isEmail(req.body.email);

// Specify allowed origins
app.use(cors({ origin: ALLOWED_DOMAINS }));

// Don't log sensitive data
console.log('User created:', user.id);

// Use async/await
const data = await fs.promises.readFile(file);
```

