## Common Attack Scenarios & Prevention

### Scenario 1: SQL Injection

**Attack:**
```
GET /users?id=1 OR 1=1
```

**Prevention:**
```javascript
app.get('/users',
  query('id').isInt().toInt(),  // Validate as integer only
  (req, res) => {
    const errors = validationResult(req);
    if (!errors.isEmpty()) return res.status(400).json({ errors });

    // Use parameterized queries
    db.query('SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ?', [req.query.id]);
  }
);
```

### Scenario 2: XSS Attack

**Attack:**
```
POST /comment body: <script>alert('xss')</script>
```

**Prevention:**
```javascript
const xss = require('xss');

app.post('/comment',
  body('text').trim().escape(),  // escape HTML
  (req, res) => {
    const safe = xss(req.body.text);
    db.saveComment(safe);
  }
);
```

### Scenario 3: Brute Force Attack

**Attack:** 1000 login attempts per minute

**Prevention:**
```javascript
const authLimiter = rateLimit({
  windowMs: 15 * 60 * 1000,
  max: 5,  // 5 attempts max
  message: 'Too many login attempts',
});

app.post('/login', authLimiter, (req, res) => {
  // Login logic
});
```

### Scenario 4: Token Theft

**Attack:** Replay intercepted JWT token

**Prevention:**
```javascript
// 1. Use HTTPS only (prevents interception)
if (NODE_ENV === 'production') {
  app.use((req, res, next) => {
    if (req.header('x-forwarded-proto') !== 'https') {
      res.redirect(`https://${req.header('host')}${req.url}`);
    } else {
      next();
    }
  });
}

// 2. Token expiration
const token = jwt.sign(user, SECRET, { expiresIn: '1h' });

// 3. Refresh token pattern
app.post('/refresh-token', (req, res) => {
  const newToken = jwt.sign(user, SECRET, { expiresIn: '1h' });
  res.json({ token: newToken });
});
```

### Scenario 5: DoS Attack

**Attack:** Send 10MB payload

**Prevention:**
```javascript
app.use(express.json({ limit: '10kb' }));
app.use(express.urlencoded({ limit: '10kb' }));
```

### Scenario 6: CSRF Attack

**Attack:** Trick user into state-changing action

**Prevention:**
```javascript
