  // Handle file
});
```

---

## Production Deployment Checklist

- [ ] Set NODE_ENV=production
- [ ] Use HTTPS/TLS with valid certificates
- [ ] Set all required environment variables
- [ ] Enable rate limiting
- [ ] Enable CORS with specific origins only
- [ ] Use helmet with CSP
- [ ] Implement authentication on all sensitive endpoints
- [ ] Add request logging and monitoring
- [ ] Use security scanning tools (npm audit, snyk)
- [ ] Set up WAF (Web Application Firewall)
- [ ] Implement API versioning (/api/v1/)
- [ ] Set up proper error monitoring (Sentry, etc.)
- [ ] Regular security audits
- [ ] Incident response plan

---

## Testing Security

```bash
# Audit dependencies
npm audit
npm audit --audit-level=high

# Check for vulnerable packages
npx snyk test

# Run tests
npm test

# Security headers check
curl -I https://yourapp.com/health
# Should have security headers

# CORS testing
curl -H "Origin: https://malicious.com" https://yourapp.com/api
# Should reject unauthorized origins
```

---

## Monitoring and Logging

```javascript
const logger = require('pino')({
  level: process.env.LOG_LEVEL || 'info',
  transport: {
    target: 'pino-pretty',
    options: {
      colorize: true,
    },
  },
});

// Log security events
logger.warn({
  event: 'failed_login_attempt',
  username: req.body.username,
  ip: req.ip,
  timestamp: new Date(),
});

// Monitor rate limiting
logger.info({
  event: 'rate_limit_exceeded',
  ip: req.ip,
  endpoint: req.path,
});

// Log successful auth
logger.info({
  event: 'user_authenticated',
  userId: req.user.id,
  ip: req.ip,
  timestamp: new Date(),
});
```

---

## Security Scanning Tools

### npm audit
```bash
npm audit
npm audit fix
npm audit fix --force # Use with caution
```

### Snyk
```bash
npm install -g snyk
snyk auth
snyk test
snyk monitor
```

### OWASP ZAP
- Automated security scanning
- Install: https://www.zaproxy.org/

### SonarQube
- Code quality and security analysis
- Setup: https://www.sonarqube.org/

---

## Security Best Practices Summary

1. **Never hardcode secrets** - Use environment variables
2. **Always validate input** - Use express-validator
3. **Implement authentication** - Use JWT or OAuth2
4. **Use HTTPS everywhere** - Enforce in production
5. **Set security headers** - Use helmet
6. **Rate limit endpoints** - Prevent brute force attacks
7. **Log security events** - Monitor for incidents
8. **Keep dependencies updated** - Run npm audit regularly
9. **Use password hashing** - Use bcrypt
10. **Handle errors safely** - Don't expose stack traces

---

## Common Vulnerabilities to Avoid

### SQL Injection
```javascript
// ❌ BAD
db.query(`SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ${id}`);

// ✅ GOOD
db.query('SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ?', [id]);
```

### XSS (Cross-Site Scripting)
```javascript
// ❌ BAD
res.send(`<h1>${userInput}</h1>`);

// ✅ GOOD
const sanitize = require('sanitize-html');
res.send(`<h1>${sanitize(userInput)}</h1>`);
```

### CSRF
```javascript
// ✅ USE CSRF TOKEN
app.use(csrf());

// In forms/API
<input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>">
```

### Broken Authentication
```javascript
// ✅ DO
- Hash passwords with bcrypt
- Use JWT with short expiration
- Validate tokens on every request
- Implement rate limiting on login
```

### Insecure Deserialization
```javascript
// ❌ BAD
eval(userInput);
Function(userInput)();

// ✅ GOOD
JSON.parse(userInput); // With try-catch
```

