#### **3. ⚠️ HIGH: Missing Security Headers (OWASP A05:2021 - Security Misconfiguration)**
**Severity:** HIGH

**Issue:**
The application doesn't set critical security headers, leaving it vulnerable to various attacks (XSS, Clickjacking, MIME-type sniffing, etc.).

**Recommendation:**

```javascript
const helmet = require('helmet');
const cors = require('cors');

// Add security headers
app.use(helmet());

// Configure CORS properly (don't use wildcards in production)
const corsOptions = {
  origin: process.env.ALLOWED_ORIGINS?.split(',') || ['https://example.com'],
  credentials: true,
  methods: ['GET', 'POST', 'PUT', 'DELETE'],
  allowedHeaders: ['Content-Type', 'Authorization'],
  maxAge: 3600, // 1 hour
};
app.use(cors(corsOptions));

// Additional security headers
app.use((req, res, next) => {
  res.setHeader('X-Content-Type-Options', 'nosniff');
  res.setHeader('X-Frame-Options', 'DENY');
  res.setHeader('X-XSS-Protection', '1; mode=block');
  res.setHeader('Strict-Transport-Security', 'max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains');
  res.setHeader('Content-Security-Policy', "default-src 'self'");
  next();
});
```

