## 🔄 Comparison Table

| Aspect | BEFORE (❌) | AFTER (✅) |
|--------|-----------|-----------|
| **Storage** | Plaintext disk file | Encrypted AWS Secrets Manager |
| **Access Control** | None (anyone can read) | IAM roles only |
| **Audit Trail** | No | Full CloudTrail logging |
| **Encryption** | None | KMS encryption at rest |
| **Rotation** | Manual, error-prone | Automated policies |
| **Version Control** | In Git history | Never in version control |
| **Environment Separation** | Mixed in one file | Separate per environment |
| **Fail Fast** | No, crashes at runtime | Yes, fails at startup |
| **Logging Safety** | Secrets leak in logs | Secrets never logged |
| **Compliance** | Non-compliant | Compliant (OWASP, PCI, HIPAA) |

---

## 🔐 Security Improvements

### Authentication & Authorization
```
BEFORE: Anyone with file access can see all secrets
AFTER:  Only EC2 instances with correct IAM role can access
```

### Data Protection
```
BEFORE: Plaintext secrets visible in file/memory/logs
AFTER:  Encrypted at rest, masked in logs, TLS in transit
```

### Audit & Compliance
```
BEFORE: No audit trail, no accountability
AFTER:  Full CloudTrail audit log of who accessed what when
```

### Incident Response
```
BEFORE: Leaked key? Manually rotate everywhere
AFTER:  Leaked key? One rotation command, immediate effect
```

---

