================================================================================
                    APP.JS SECURITY REVIEW - FINDINGS & RECOMMENDATIONS
================================================================================

APPLICATION OVERVIEW:
- Framework: Express.js
- Endpoints: /health, /users
- Port: 3000
- Functionality: Simple health check and user list endpoint

================================================================================
VULNERABILITIES IDENTIFIED
================================================================================

1. MISSING AUTHENTICATION & AUTHORIZATION (OWASP A01:2021 - Broken Access Control)
   ⚠️  SEVERITY: CRITICAL

   ISSUE:
   - No authentication mechanism on any endpoints
   - No authorization checks
   - Sensitive user data (emails) exposed without verification
   - Anyone can access the /users endpoint

   AFFECTED CODE:
   ```
   app.get('/users', (req, res) => {
     res.json([
       { id: 1, name: 'Alice', email: 'alice@example.com' },
       { id: 2, name: 'Bob', email: 'bob@example.com' },
     ]);
   });
   ```

   RECOMMENDATIONS:
   a) Implement authentication middleware (JWT, OAuth2, or sessions)
   b) Add authorization checks based on user roles
   c) Implement rate limiting
   d) Add request validation

   SECURE IMPLEMENTATION EXAMPLE:
   ```javascript
   const jwt = require('jsonwebtoken');
   const rateLimit = require('express-rate-limit');

   // Middleware for authentication
   const authenticateToken = (req, res, next) => {
     const authHeader = req.headers['authorization'];
     const token = authHeader && authHeader.split(' ')[1];

     if (!token) {
       return res.status(401).json({ error: 'Access token required' });
     }

     jwt.verify(token, process.env.JWT_SECRET, (err, user) => {
       if (err) {
         return res.status(403).json({ error: 'Invalid token' });
       }
       req.user = user;
       next();
     });
   };

   // Rate limiting
   const limiter = rateLimit({
     windowMs: 15 * 60 * 1000, // 15 minutes
     max: 100 // limit each IP to 100 requests per windowMs
   });

   app.use(limiter);

   // Protected endpoint
   app.get('/users', authenticateToken, (req, res) => {
     // Only authorized users can access
     if (req.user.role !== 'admin' && req.user.role !== 'user') {
       return res.status(403).json({ error: 'Unauthorized' });
     }
     res.json([
       { id: 1, name: 'Alice', email: 'alice@example.com' },
       { id: 2, name: 'Bob', email: 'bob@example.com' },
     ]);
   });
   ```

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

2. NO INPUT VALIDATION (OWASP A03:2021 - Injection)
   ⚠️  SEVERITY: HIGH

   ISSUE:
   - No validation of incoming requests
   - Query parameters not sanitized
   - Potential vector for injection attacks
   - No schema validation

   POTENTIAL ATTACK:
   GET /users?search=<img src=x onerror="alert('xss')">

   RECOMMENDATIONS:
   a) Use input validation middleware (express-validator)
   b) Define strict schemas for all inputs
   c) Sanitize all user inputs
   d) Implement whitelist validation

   SECURE IMPLEMENTATION EXAMPLE:
   ```javascript
   const { query, validationResult } = require('express-validator');
   const mongoSanitize = require('express-mongo-sanitize');

   // Sanitize data against NoSQL injection
   app.use(mongoSanitize());

   // Input validation for /users endpoint
   app.get('/users',
     authenticateToken,
     query('limit').optional().isInt({ min: 1, max: 100 }).toInt(),
     query('offset').optional().isInt({ min: 0 }).toInt(),
     query('search').optional().trim().isLength({ max: 50 }),
     (req, res) => {
       // Check for validation errors
       const errors = validationResult(req);
       if (!errors.isEmpty()) {
         return res.status(400).json({ errors: errors.array() });
       }

       const { limit = 10, offset = 0, search } = req.query;

       // Process safely validated inputs
       let users = [
         { id: 1, name: 'Alice', email: 'alice@example.com' },
         { id: 2, name: 'Bob', email: 'bob@example.com' },
       ];

       if (search) {
         users = users.filter(u => 
           u.name.toLowerCase().includes(search.toLowerCase())
         );
       }

       res.json(users.slice(offset, offset + limit));
     }
   );
   ```

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

3. NO HTTPS / TLS ENFORCEMENT (OWASP A02:2021 - Cryptographic Failures)
   ⚠️  SEVERITY: CRITICAL

   ISSUE:
   - Application runs on HTTP only
   - No TLS/SSL encryption
   - Credentials transmitted in plaintext
   - Vulnerable to man-in-the-middle attacks

   RECOMMENDATIONS:
   a) Always use HTTPS in production
   b) Implement HSTS headers
   c) Use secure cookies
   d) Enforce TLS 1.2+

   SECURE IMPLEMENTATION EXAMPLE:
   ```javascript
   const https = require('https');
   const fs = require('fs');
   const helmet = require('helmet');

   // Enable security headers
   app.use(helmet());

   // Enforce HTTPS redirect in production
   app.use((req, res, next) => {
     if (process.env.NODE_ENV === 'production' && !req.secure) {
       return res.redirect(`https://${req.headers.host}${req.url}`);
     }
     next();
   });

   // HSTS header (already included with helmet)
   // Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains

   // Production: Use HTTPS
   if (process.env.NODE_ENV === 'production') {
     const options = {
       key: fs.readFileSync(process.env.SSL_KEY_PATH),
       cert: fs.readFileSync(process.env.SSL_CERT_PATH)
     };
     https.createServer(options, app).listen(443);
   } else {
     app.listen(3000);
   }
   ```

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

4. MISSING SECURITY HEADERS (OWASP A01:2021)
   ⚠️  SEVERITY: MEDIUM

   ISSUE:
   - No Content Security Policy (CSP)
   - No X-Frame-Options (clickjacking)
   - No X-Content-Type-Options (MIME sniffing)
   - No X-XSS-Protection
   - Vulnerable to various client-side attacks

   RECOMMENDATIONS:
   Use helmet.js middleware

   SECURE IMPLEMENTATION EXAMPLE:
   ```javascript
   const helmet = require('helmet');

   // Apply security headers
   app.use(helmet());

   // Additional custom headers
   app.use((req, res, next) => {
     res.setHeader('X-Content-Type-Options', 'nosniff');
     res.setHeader('X-Frame-Options', 'DENY');
     res.setHeader('X-XSS-Protection', '1; mode=block');
     res.setHeader('Content-Security-Policy', "default-src 'self'");
     res.setHeader('Referrer-Policy', 'strict-origin-when-cross-origin');
     next();
   });
   ```

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

5. NO ERROR HANDLING / INFORMATION DISCLOSURE (OWASP A01:2021)
   ⚠️  SEVERITY: MEDIUM

   ISSUE:
   - No centralized error handling
   - Stack traces may be exposed to clients
   - No logging mechanism
   - Unhandled exceptions could crash the server

   RECOMMENDATIONS:
   a) Implement centralized error handling
   b) Log errors securely
   c) Return generic error messages to clients
   d) Never expose stack traces in production

   SECURE IMPLEMENTATION EXAMPLE:
   ```javascript
   const winston = require('winston');

   // Setup logging
   const logger = winston.createLogger({
     level: 'info',
     format: winston.format.json(),
     transports: [
       new winston.transports.File({ filename: 'error.log', level: 'error' }),
       new winston.transports.File({ filename: 'combined.log' })
     ]
   });

   if (process.env.NODE_ENV !== 'production') {
     logger.add(new winston.transports.Console({
       format: winston.format.simple()
     }));
   }

   // Centralized error handler
   app.use((err, req, res, next) => {
     logger.error({
       message: err.message,
       stack: err.stack,
       path: req.path,
       method: req.method
     });

     // Don't expose error details in production
     const errorResponse = {
       message: process.env.NODE_ENV === 'production' 
         ? 'Internal Server Error' 
         : err.message
     };

     res.status(err.status || 500).json(errorResponse);
   });

   // Catch unhandled rejections
   process.on('unhandledRejection', (reason, promise) => {
     logger.error('Unhandled Rejection:', reason);
   });
   ```

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

6. NO CORS CONFIGURATION (OWASP A01:2021)
   ⚠️  SEVERITY: MEDIUM

   ISSUE:
   - No explicit CORS policy defined
   - Potential for unauthorized cross-origin requests
   - Default behavior allows all origins

   RECOMMENDATIONS:
   a) Implement strict CORS policy
   b) Whitelist allowed origins
   c) Restrict allowed methods
   d) Validate preflight requests

   SECURE IMPLEMENTATION EXAMPLE:
   ```javascript
   const cors = require('cors');

   // Configure CORS
   const corsOptions = {
     origin: process.env.ALLOWED_ORIGINS?.split(',') || ['http://localhost:3000'],
     credentials: true,
     methods: ['GET', 'POST'],
     allowedHeaders: ['Content-Type', 'Authorization'],
     maxAge: 86400 // 24 hours
   };

   app.use(cors(corsOptions));

   // Handle preflight
   app.options('*', cors(corsOptions));
   ```

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

7. HARDCODED SENSITIVE DATA (OWASP A02:2021)
   ⚠️  SEVERITY: MEDIUM

   ISSUE:
   - Email addresses exposed in source code
   - No environment configuration
   - Secrets not managed securely

   RECOMMENDATIONS:
   a) Use environment variables
   b) Use .env files (development only)
   c) Never commit sensitive data
   d) Use secrets management systems (AWS Secrets Manager, HashiCorp Vault)

   SECURE IMPLEMENTATION EXAMPLE:
   ```javascript
   require('dotenv').config();

   app.get('/users', authenticateToken, (req, res) => {
     // Load user data from database, not hardcoded
     const users = getUsersFromDatabase();
     res.json(users);
   });
   ```

   .env file (never commit):
   ```
   DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:pass@localhost/dbname
   JWT_SECRET=your-secret-key-here
   API_KEYS=key1,key2,key3
   ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://yourdomain.com
   ```

   .gitignore:
   ```
   .env
   .env.local
   *.key
   *.pem
   ```

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

8. NO RATE LIMITING / DOS PROTECTION (OWASP A01:2021)
   ⚠️  SEVERITY: MEDIUM

   ISSUE:
   - No rate limiting on endpoints
   - Vulnerable to Denial of Service (DoS) attacks
   - No brute force protection

   (See RECOMMENDATION #1 for implementation example)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

9. MISSING DEPENDENCY SECURITY (Supply Chain)
   ⚠️  SEVERITY: MEDIUM

   ISSUE:
   - No package.json visible - cannot assess dependency versions
   - No security audit baseline
   - Potential vulnerable dependencies

   RECOMMENDATIONS:
   a) Run: npm audit
   b) Keep dependencies up to date
   c) Use npm audit in CI/CD pipeline
   d) Review node version for LTS

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

10. NO VALIDATION OF HTTP METHODS (OWASP A01:2021)
    ⚠️  SEVERITY: LOW

    ISSUE:
    - No checks for unexpected HTTP methods
    - Could receive POST, PUT, DELETE on GET-only endpoints

    RECOMMENDATIONS:
    Use middleware to validate methods

    EXAMPLE:
    ```javascript
    app.all('/users', (req, res, next) => {
      if (!['GET'].includes(req.method)) {
        return res.status(405).json({ error: 'Method Not Allowed' });
      }
      next();
    });
    ```

================================================================================
RECOMMENDED SECURE APPLICATION STRUCTURE
================================================================================

