- [ ] Curl with invalid token: `curl -H "Authorization: Bearer invalid" ...`
- [ ] Check headers: `curl -I https://your-app.com`
- [ ] Test rate limiting: Run repeated requests quickly
- [ ] Test injection: `curl "...?id=1 OR 1=1"`
- [ ] Test XSS: `curl "...?q=<script>alert(1)</script>"`

### Automated Testing
```bash
# Run all tests
npm test

# Run security tests only
npm test -- app_secure.test.js

# Check for vulnerabilities
npm audit
npx snyk test

# Check for exposed secrets
npx gitleaks detect

# Lint
npx eslint .
```

### Tools for Testing
- **OWASP ZAP:** Free security scanner
- **Burp Suite:** Professional penetration testing
- **npm audit:** Check for vulnerable dependencies
- **Snyk:** Continuous vulnerability monitoring
- **SonarQube:** Code quality & security
- **Dependabot:** Automated dependency updates

## Environment Setup

### Development (.env.development)
```
NODE_ENV=development
PORT=3000
JWT_SECRET=dev-secret-not-secure
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000
```

### Production (.env.production)
```
NODE_ENV=production
PORT=3000
JWT_SECRET=<32-character-random-secret>
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://example.com,https://app.example.com
```

### Generating Strong Secrets
```bash
# Generate 32-character random secret
node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"

# Or use openssl
openssl rand -base64 32
```

## Response Status Codes

| Code | Meaning | Use Case |
|---|---|---|
| 200 | OK | Successful request |
| 400 | Bad Request | Invalid input parameters |
| 401 | Unauthorized | Missing/invalid authentication |
| 403 | Forbidden | Valid auth but insufficient permissions |
| 404 | Not Found | Resource doesn't exist |
| 429 | Too Many Requests | Rate limit exceeded |
| 500 | Internal Error | Server error (don't expose details) |

