  --secret-id app/jwt-secret \
  --version-id PREVIOUS_VERSION_ID
```

### 4. Implement Secret Expiration
```javascript
class SecretWithExpiration {
  constructor(value, expirationDays = 90) {
    this.value = value;
    this.createdAt = new Date();
    this.expirationDays = expirationDays;
  }

  isExpired() {
    const expirationDate = new Date(this.createdAt);
    expirationDate.setDate(expirationDate.getDate() + this.expirationDays);
    return new Date() > expirationDate;
  }

  getAge() {
    const now = new Date();
    const ageInDays = Math.floor((now - this.createdAt) / (1000 * 60 * 60 * 24));
    return ageInDays;
  }

  warnIfExpiringSoon() {
    const daysUntilExpiration = this.expirationDays - this.getAge();
    if (daysUntilExpiration <= 7) {
      console.warn(`⚠️  Secret expires in ${daysUntilExpiration} days`);
    }
  }
}
```

### 5. Use Environment-Specific Secrets
```
Production: AWS Secrets Manager
Staging: Separate AWS account
Development: .env files (local only)
Testing: In-memory secrets
```

